{"availability":"available","full":"kincoy/cc9s","name":"cc9s","description":"A k9s-inspired CLI and TUI for managing Claude Code sessions — browse, search, inspect, and clean up your AI coding sessions","category":"Productivity","language":"Go","stars":65,"forks":5,"created":"2026-03-22T08:24:15Z","updated":"2026-04-27T07:56:07Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["ai","ai-coding","ai-tools","claude","claude-code","cli","command-line","developer-tools","go","golang","productivity","session-management","session-manager","terminal","terminal-ui","tui"],"demo":"https://asciinema.org/a/vABD89zAYT8G7Y6C","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:00.548Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:00.548Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:00.548Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T18:01:00.548Z","stars":65,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A k9s-inspired TUI for managing Claude Code sessions, skills, and agents","Claude Code stores session data as JSONL files under /.claude/. When you accumulate hundreds of sessions across dozens of projects, finding and managing them becomes painful.","cc9s solves this by providing a full-screen terminal UI — inspired by k9s — that lets you browse, search, inspect, and resume sessions, and inspect local Claude Code skills and agents, without leaving your keyboard."],"features":["Two-level navigation — Projects → Sessions, drill down with Enter, go back with Esc","Project overview — See local project session, skill, command, and agent summaries, then inspect project paths and local Claude roots with d","Session resume — Jump directly into a Claude Code session from the TUI","Search & filter — / to search, :context to filter by project","Batch delete — Space to select, x to delete multiple sessions"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kincoy/cc9s/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8bb3520d1f32ef171203d4308ee15ea7fe8486bf8308f55c611f36b053195aec","extr